content.en:
**Two-Box Thinking**
&nbsp;  

To understand where we are going, we must look at the Two Box Model:

&nbsp;  

**Box 1 (Optimization):** This is still everything you do today, but now you apply **Agentic Workflows** and **Custom Agents.** Instead of manually prompting an AI for every single task, you build "Specialists" to automate entire repeatable processes, drastically compressing time and reducing costs

&nbsp;  

**Box 2 (Possibility):** This is where you use **Hydration** and **Product Scaffolding.** You can now take a tiny input (like a 5-minute conversation) and expand it into massive artifacts—project plans, prototypes, and specifications—creating value that was previously too complex or expensive to generate manually

&nbsp;  

**The Goal:** We use Level 2 skills (Orchestration and the **Rule of Three**) to turn manual work in Box 1 into automated "assembly lines," freeing us to architect entirely new solutions in Box 2

