If Level 2 was about mastering the assembly line, **Level 3 is about designing and building the factory itself.**

&nbsp; 

This is why your **Maximalist Journey** had to take you through the rigours of Levels 1 and 2. You cannot function as an Architect—**the person designing the facility**—if you don't understand the machinery inside it.

&nbsp; 

**Level 1** was your training on the raw materials—learning how to shape instructions with RICECO.

