We have covered the frameworks, the mindsets, and the workflows. But an Orchestrator who never lifts their baton is just a person standing in a quiet room.

&nbsp; 

To truly graduate from Level 2, you need to put this into practice. So, we are leaving you with three 'First Quests.' I want you to pick one of these to tackle before we meet again.

&nbsp; 

**Quest 1 is The Meeting Multiplier**. This is your quick win. Take the transcript from your next team meeting and use an agentic workflow to 'hydrate' it. Don't just summarize it—turn it into a project plan, a risk register, and a stakeholder email. Do in 5 minutes what usually takes you an hour.

&nbsp; 

**Quest 2 is The Process Documenter**. This is for the system thinkers. Take a core process your team does every week and map it out. Build the agents that can do each step. Create a 'digital twin' of your business logic.

&nbsp; 

**Quest 3 is The Knowledge Curator**. This is for the architects at heart. Take that folder of messy documents or that process that only lives in your head—your tacit knowledge—and structure it into a mini-knowledge bank that an AI can actually use.

&nbsp; 

You have the tools. You have the RICECO framework. You understand the Assembly Line. **The only thing left to do is start.**

&nbsp;

content.fr:
Nous avons couvert les cadres, les mentalités, et les workflows. Mais un Orchestrateur qui ne lève jamais sa baguette n'est qu'une personne debout dans une pièce silencieuse.

